Prophecy has been given, whether the word is simple or the teaching is put forth in parables. But pay attention to what other agreements you receive concerning the army and strategy of the one who sends. You will be handed over to councils, but take courage, the Father is not separated, the Son is not distant, the Spirit does not depart, angels are your bodyguards. You will be flogged in their synagogues, but you should greatly rejoice. For the wars on behalf of piety and the bruises from the whips are more becoming than the sun's rays. You will be brought before rulers and kings because of me as a testimony to them and the nations. Do not become numb to this. On my account, you stand before rulers, you are brought before kings for the sake of my glory. The one who anointed kings, who set boundaries for rulers, who measured their step and gave them a scepter, is with you. Consider this, that you are not led before kings and rulers as captives, but as a testimony to them, and to the nations, so that they may know the power of the one testified to by you, that the poor restrain the rulers, the rustic people intimidate the imperial council and silence the renowned senate, the private citizens shame the tyrants and intimidate the kings. When you are handed over, do not worry about what you will say.

For you are tongues of the word and wisdom, and trumpets and heralds of life, and orators of the one who does not need oration, and for this reason what follows you is; For it will be given to you in that hour what to say; Before the hour, the word of grace is not supplied to you, lest you think the words brought by you are yours; For you are not the ones speaking, but the spirit of your father speaking in you; The struggle and contest are for his sake; The stadium is for his sake; It is necessary to wait for grace from him, to expect the word, to receive the gift of confession, to hope for the full armor, against which the enemy cannot prevail, because it is forged by God; A brother will hand over a brother to death, and a father his child, and children will rise up against parents and kill them; Nature is divided, and grace is gathered; The clay fights against itself, but the potter does not tolerate handing over the clay; The earthenware vessels are crushed together, so that in the need of the potter's wheel they may become such, and thus they take on the memory of the potter and are taken by necessity; You will be hated by all because of my name; It is enough for you for glory, sufficient for dignity, not small for confidence, that you are hated by all; The one who is above all does not tolerate betraying you, but perseveres, loving and warming the love more; You will be hated by all because of my name;

The one enduring to the end will be saved. Hear the word, O faithful, and keep the commandment and cultivate endurance with eagerness and reap the fruit of it with great joy. Gather the grape, tread the winepress. Do not say many things: the terrible things are varied, the sorrowful things are difficult, the continuous things are gloomy; the things from one's homeland are delightful, but the things in a foreign land are hateful; the ones comforting are few, but the ones mocking are many; philosophy is blasphemed and virtue is scorned; fear concerning one's own things holds me, a struggle from relatives has come upon me, the care of one's own things besieges me. Do not say these things, do not think them, and do not loosen the nerves of endurance, nor cultivate laziness within yourself, but eagerly look to this royal cross, gaze at it and examine this holy pasture, the Resurrection, with it. Depict to yourself the king hanging on a tree, the master unjustly struck by slaves, the lawgiver shamelessly spat upon by the guilty, the one clothed in all the wealth of attire shamelessly stripped; but behold, you see the Resurrection in what? Here the garments of the stripped one show his wealth, the angels will present the power of the one struck, the voices of those coming from heaven proclaim the glory of the one slapped; glory to him now and forever and to the ages of ages. Amen.
